## 3. Target Audience & Positioning

**Primary buyer:** Corporate L&D / Training Managers and HR leaders at mid-to-large organizations who currently juggle spreadsheets, a generic LMS, calendar invites, and WhatsApp/email for what should be one connected workflow.

**Positioning statement:**
*"TrainHub360 is the training platform corporates actually asked for: one that proves training worked, deploys in days instead of years, and scales predictably without an enterprise implementation tax."*

The wedge against incumbents (Docebo, Cornerstone, Absorb, TalentLMS, Litmos, 360Learning) isn't just feature parity — it's agility and structural alignment:

1. **Deploy in Days, Not Years:** Unlike legacy systems that require 12–24 month implementations and expensive third-party consultants, TrainHub360 is built for immediate, self-serve mid-market deployment.
2. **Purpose-built for internal staff training** (not customer education or academic use), so the data model matches how corporates run programmes: org → programme → administrator → trainer → cohort → learner.


3. **Predictable, Transparent Scaling:** No bloated enterprise minimums, hidden module fees, or opaque renewal surprises.
4. **Manager-facing KPI dashboards from day one**, not an add-on analytics module.


5. **Competence over completion** baked into the assessment engine.


6. Multi-org, multi-tenant from the ground up (an organization registers, manages its own users, branding, and data boundary).



---

## 4. User Roles & Core Workflows

| Role | Who | Core capabilities |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Organization Owner (IT/SysAdmin)** | The corporate account holder | Registers the org, manages SSO/SAML integrations, sets up billing/branding, manages global security policies, and views org-wide KPI rollups. *Strictly separated from training content to ensure data security.*

 |
| **Training Programme Administrator** | Appointed per programme | Adds/removes trainers and learners, creates courses, manages enrolments, sets certification/compliance rules, and owns programme-level reporting.

 |
| **Trainer** | Subject-matter expert / facilitator | Uploads course material, links external courses, schedules sessions (online/offline), sends invitations, grades assessments, runs 1:1s, messages learners.

 |
| **Learner** | Employee | Views assigned courses, tracks progress, takes tests, sees results, books 1:1 sessions, DMs trainers, manages their schedule.

 |
| **Stakeholder (view-only)** | Department head, exec sponsor | Read-only dashboards scoped to their department/cohort — no editing rights.

 |

A single person can hold more than one role (e.g., a Trainer who is also a Programme Administrator) — role assignment is per-programme, not global, so permissions don't leak across programmes an org runs concurrently.

